1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:07,480
Chat sends the spirits. Your
shadow guards the light.

2
00:00:07,480 --> 00:00:10,650
This is Khayal: a shadow
theatre built for Twitch,

3
00:00:10,650 --> 00:00:12,600
where the audience takes the puppets

4
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:15,320
and the streamer steps inside the performance.

5
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:18,790
The idea comes from Egyptian
shadow theatre: a lamp,

6
00:00:18,790 --> 00:00:22,120
a screen, and figures
brought to life by people.

7
00:00:22,120 --> 00:00:25,580
Khayal brings that shared
performance into a stream,

8
00:00:25,580 --> 00:00:29,060
with a camera silhouette and
puppets controlled through chat.

9
00:00:29,060 --> 00:00:30,990
A viewer summons a cat or a camel,

10
00:00:30,990 --> 00:00:33,010
then moves it with simple commands.

11
00:00:33,010 --> 00:00:34,260
Pull it toward the lamp

12
00:00:34,260 --> 00:00:36,280
and the shadow grows larger and softer.

13
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:38,580
Each puppet belongs to one viewer,

14
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:40,840
with a queue when the stage fills.

15
00:00:40,840 --> 00:00:45,380
Then comes Afreet Hunt.
Sixty seconds. Five lanterns.

16
00:00:45,380 --> 00:00:48,280
Chat sends spirits toward
the lights while the streamer

17
00:00:48,280 --> 00:00:50,680
tries to swat them away
with a changing silhouette.

18
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:53,420
Keep at least three lanterns burning to win.

19
00:00:53,420 --> 00:00:56,080
The camera reads movement along your outline,

20
00:00:56,080 --> 00:00:57,990
so a still shadow is not a hit.

21
00:00:57,990 --> 00:01:00,960
A separate cue book lets the
streamer direct the show.

22
00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:02,870
Rehearsal is clearly labeled,

23
00:01:02,870 --> 00:01:05,720
so simulated events stay separate from Twitch.

24
00:01:05,720 --> 00:01:09,000
Captions are cleaned, commands have cooldowns,

25
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:12,050
and stage moderation stays
under the broadcaster's control.

26
00:01:12,050 --> 00:01:15,040
When the curtain falls, a
playbill credits the cast.

27
00:01:15,040 --> 00:01:17,980
The goal is a small shared performance:

28
00:01:17,980 --> 00:01:20,360
an unexpected giant cat, a desperate save,

29
00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:22,530
and a record of who helped make the night.

30
00:01:22,530 --> 00:01:25,220
I directed the concept and used Codex

31
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:27,640
to build the TypeScript app, command handling,

32
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:31,140
cue book, Twitch connection
code, and camera worker.

33
00:01:31,140 --> 00:01:34,520
Pixi draws the theatre; MediaPipe
supplies the silhouette.

34
00:01:34,520 --> 00:01:36,920
Tests check the rules, while real camera

35
00:01:36,920 --> 00:01:39,530
and Twitch recordings must
prove the performance.

36
00:01:39,530 --> 00:01:41,400
Khayal gives chat a part to play

37
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:43,590
and the streamer a stage to inhabit.

38
00:01:43,590 --> 00:01:45,930
Bring your shadow. Guard the light.

39
00:01:45,930 --> 00:01:48,480
Come back tomorrow. There is more to see.
